# UI / UX
- Preserve established visual language, spacing, typography, component patterns and navigation unless redesign is requested.
- Do not introduce unrelated visual redesign during functional work.
- Keep layouts responsive for supported screens/windows and text scaling.
- Preserve localization and correct RTL/LTR directionality; avoid hard-coded translated-text-breaking assumptions.
- Maintain accessibility semantics, labels, focus order, keyboard support and adequate targets where supported.
- Implement relevant loading, empty, error, disabled, retry, offline and success states.
- Avoid duplicate UI state and unnecessary rebuild/re-render; follow existing state architecture.
- Never hide failures behind indefinite spinners or silent fallbacks.
- Reuse existing design-system components before creating duplicates.
- Preserve user input/data through transient errors when practical.
- Update/add golden/screenshot/widget/component tests only for intentional visual behavior changes.
